{
  "matches": [
    {
      "refs": [
        "action:n2"
      ],
      "verbatim_texts": [
        "For TS recruitment, the first step is to advise unsuccessful candidates."
      ],
      "justification": "Init captures the implicit process start; action n2 faithfully restates the first operational step."
    },
    {
      "refs": [
        "action:n3",
        "guard:b1->n4",
        "action:n4",
        "guard:b1->n6"
      ],
      "verbatim_texts": [
        "If there are \"no more candidates\", then the position should be re-advertised."
      ],
      "justification": "Elements model the conditional check, positive branch (re-advertise), and negative branch flow."
    },
    {
      "refs": [
        "action:n6",
        "guard:b2->n7",
        "action:n7",
        "guard:b2->c1"
      ],
      "verbatim_texts": [
        "However, if the terms and conditions of the offer for a candidate need to be sorted out, it is necessary to check if the candidate has accepted a voluntary redundancy."
      ],
      "justification": "Models the T&C check condition and transition to the voluntary redundancy verification."
    },
    {
      "refs": [
        "guard:b3->n8",
        "action:n8"
      ],
      "verbatim_texts": [
        "On the other hand, if the candidate has accepted, further investigation is required."
      ],
      "justification": "Captures the accepted branch leading to the investigation step."
    },
    {
      "refs": [
        "guard:b3->c1"
      ],
      "verbatim_texts": [
        "If the candidate has not accepted, the process continues."
      ],
      "justification": "Guard correctly routes the non-accepted path to continuation."
    },
    {
      "refs": [
        "action:n11",
        "action:n12"
      ],
      "verbatim_texts": [
        "The recruitment manager sends an Appointment Approval form, which is then received by the next level manager."
      ],
      "justification": "Two actions accurately split the sending and receiving phases."
    },
    {
      "refs": [
        "action:n13",
        "guard:b4->n14",
        "action:n14",
        "guard:b4->n16"
      ],
      "verbatim_texts": [
        "If the manager is an external resource, they may not authorize the form."
      ],
      "justification": "Branch and guards handle the external resource condition (modeled as inverse of existing employee) and its authorization consequence."
    },
    {
      "refs": [
        "action:n16",
        "guard:b5->n19",
        "action:n19",
        "action:n20",
        "guard:b5->n17"
      ],
      "verbatim_texts": [
        "However, if the approver is an existing employee of the client, the process continues. If the form is approved, the recruitment manager sends the form and other documentation, which is received by the client HR."
      ],
      "justification": "Elements split the employee check and form approval condition, covering doc transmission, reception, and negative routing."
    },
    {
      "refs": [
        "action:n21"
      ],
      "verbatim_texts": [
        "The HR department scans the completed form and records the position against the stored position in GovSource."
      ],
      "justification": "Directly restates the HR scanning and recording step."
    },
    {
      "refs": [
        "action:n22",
        "guard:b6->n23",
        "action:n23"
      ],
      "verbatim_texts": [
        "If there are any variations, a complete business case is required."
      ],
      "justification": "Models the variation check and subsequent business case preparation."
    },
    {
      "refs": [
        "guard:b6->c2",
        "action:n25"
      ],
      "verbatim_texts": [
        "Otherwise, the process continues. The Appointment Approval is carried forward."
      ],
      "justification": "Guard and converge manage the otherwise path; action captures carrying forward the approval."
    },
    {
      "refs": [
        "action:n26",
        "guard:b7->n27",
        "action:n27"
      ],
      "verbatim_texts": [
        "If the position requires a medical assessment, it is applicable for a 12% rate."
      ],
      "justification": "Accurately models the medical assessment requirement and associated rate."
    },
    {
      "refs": [
        "guard:b7->n28",
        "action:n28"
      ],
      "verbatim_texts": [
        "Otherwise, a medical assessment is not necessary."
      ],
      "justification": "Captures the alternative branch where assessment is bypassed."
    },
    {
      "refs": [
        "action:n29"
      ],
      "verbatim_texts": [
        "For the step of the Preferred Candidate's medical assessments, it is important to note that it can take up to 21 days to arrange and complete."
      ],
      "justification": "Restates the scheduling step and 21-day timeframe limit."
    },
    {
      "refs": [
        "action:n30",
        "action:n31"
      ],
      "verbatim_texts": [
        "The TS HR coordinator informs the recruitment manager, who then liaises with the HR representative to confirm the offer to the candidate."
      ],
      "justification": "Splits the informing and liaising activities faithfully."
    },
    {
      "refs": [
        "action:n32",
        "guard:b8->n33",
        "action:n33"
      ],
      "verbatim_texts": [
        "If the assessment is not satisfactory, the next candidate on the shortlist should be contacted."
      ],
      "justification": "Models the unsatisfactory outcome and contact step."
    },
    {
      "refs": [
        "guard:b8->n35"
      ],
      "verbatim_texts": [
        "If the assessment is not satisfactory, the next candidate on the shortlist should be contacted."
      ],
      "justification": "Implicit positive branch (satisfactory) routes to process continuation."
    },
    {
      "refs": [
        "action:n35"
      ],
      "verbatim_texts": [
        "The recruitment manager makes a formal verbal offer of employment to the candidate."
      ],
      "justification": "Directly matches the verbal offer step."
    },
    {
      "refs": [
        "action:n36",
        "guard:b9->n37",
        "action:n37"
      ],
      "verbatim_texts": [
        "If the candidate accepts, the recruitment manager creates a formal written offer."
      ],
      "justification": "Models the acceptance check and written offer creation."
    },
    {
      "refs": [
        "guard:b9->c4"
      ],
      "verbatim_texts": [
        "If the candidate declines, the process continues."
      ],
      "justification": "Routes the decline outcome to continuation."
    },
    {
      "refs": [
        "action:n39"
      ],
      "verbatim_texts": [
        "Simultaneously, the commencement pack and letter of appointment are sent to the candidate."
      ],
      "justification": "AND gateway correctly models simultaneous execution with the sending action."
    },
    {
      "refs": [
        "action:n40",
        "action:n41",
        "guard:b10->n42",
        "action:n42"
      ],
      "verbatim_texts": [
        "Once the candidate receives these documents, if there is a \"40%\" rate, renegotiation is required."
      ],
      "justification": "Covers document receipt, rate check, and renegotiation trigger."
    },
    {
      "refs": [
        "guard:b10->n47",
        "action:n47"
      ],
      "verbatim_texts": [
        "Otherwise, if the candidate accepts, the process continues."
      ],
      "justification": "Handles the alternative path without renegotiation."
    },
    {
      "refs": [
        "action:n43",
        "guard:b11->n44",
        "action:n44",
        "guard:b11->n46",
        "action:n46"
      ],
      "verbatim_texts": [
        "If the renegotiation is successful, the process continues. However, if the renegotiation is unsuccessful, the next candidate on the shortlist should be identified."
      ],
      "justification": "Fully models both success and failure outcomes of renegotiation."
    },
    {
      "refs": [
        "end:e1"
      ],
      "verbatim_texts": [
        "Finally, the process ends."
      ],
      "justification": "End node directly corresponds to the closing statement."
    }
  ],
